        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7825e170-8db3-5ab2-9d46-464d577b305b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: 1981 Oklahoma Sooners football team\n- Organizations: University of Oklahoma, Big Eight Conference, Big 12 Conference, University of Texas at Austin\n- People: Barry Switzer\n- Places: Oklahoma Memorial Stadium, Gaylord Family Oklahoma Memorial Stadium, Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium\n- Events: 1981 NCAA Division I-A football season, 2015 renovations\n\nFacts:\n- The 1981 Oklahoma Sooners football team represented the University of Oklahoma during the 1981 NCAA Division I-A football season.\n- The 1981 Oklahoma Sooners football team played its home games at Oklahoma Memorial Stadium and competed in the Big Eight Conference.\n- Barry Switzer was the head coach of the 1981 Oklahoma Sooners football team.\n- Following 2015 renovations, Gaylord Family Oklahoma Memorial Stadium had an official seating capacity of 86,112.\n- Following the 2015 renovations, Gaylord Family Oklahoma Memorial Stadium was the 23rd largest stadium in the world.\n- Following the 2015 renovations, Gaylord Family Oklahoma Memorial Stadium was the 15th largest college stadium in the United States.\n- Following the 2015 renovations, Gaylord Family Oklahoma Memorial Stadium was the second largest stadium in the Big 12 Conference, behind Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium at the University of Texas at Austin.",
